Approach: For each fruit, iterate through baskets and place it in the first basket with enough capacity, marking that basket as used.

Time Complexity: O(n²) — nested loops used for checking each fruit against baskets.

Space Complexity: O(1) — no extra data structures used.

class Solution {
    public int numOfUnplacedFruits(int[] f, int[] b) {
        int count=0;
        for(int i=0;i<f.length;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<b.length;j++){
                if(f[i]<=b[j]){
                    b[j]=0;
                    count++;
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
        return b.length-count;
    }
}
